From f6764cf6c1635a42b2fb55219afce9b9dbff78b4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 22:19:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] drm: HDR10PLUS_VSIF, the HDR10+ vendor InfoFrame of each
 frame

HDR10+ (SMPTE ST 2094-40 dynamic metadata) reaches a display in the
HDR10+ vendor-specific InfoFrame, next to the HDR one, with the
metadata of each frame. DRM has HDR_OUTPUT_METADATA for the static
metadata and nothing for this.

HDR10PLUS_VSIF is a connector blob property: the payload of that
InfoFrame (the IEEE OUI 90-84-8B and 24 bytes, 27 in all), which user
space sets with the commit that flips the frame; 0 for none. The core
creates it, checks its size and OUI, and carries it in the connector
state (duplicated and released with it, and compared by
drm_connector_atomic_hdr10plus_vsif_equal()). drm_hdr10plus.h frames
it for HDMI (the InfoFrame with its checksum) and for DisplayPort (an
InfoFrame SDP, in the form DRM drivers send the HDR one).

A driver attaches it where it sends that InfoFrame in a slot of its
own, from the commit that sets it and never as a change of mode, and
refuses a commit it cannot honour: linux-9981 (amdgpu) and linux-9982
(i915 and xe). nvidia-drm has a property of the same name and meaning
(nvidia-open-kernel-modules-9020). User space reads the sink's HDR10+
support in its EDID.

The layout of the payload is that of the HDR10+ technical
specification, which is licensed; the kernel does not interpret it.

Checked: the whole of drm compiled, W=1 without new warnings; host
test of the framing against these headers (expected bytes written out
by hand), with mutations of each check.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/drm_atomic_state_helper.c |  3 +
 drivers/gpu/drm/drm_atomic_uapi.c         | 18 +++++
 drivers/gpu/drm/drm_connector.c           | 57 ++++++++++++++++
 include/drm/drm_connector.h               | 10 +++
 include/drm/drm_hdr10plus.h               | 83 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 include/drm/drm_mode_config.h             |  6 ++
 6 files changed, 177 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 include/drm/drm_hdr10plus.h

